# The memory of everything the agent runs on a session VM: the relay with the agent and what it starts (dev servers, its
# tmux, test runs), the services of hunt.json, the gate checks of the swf runner and the desktop's Chromium. The VM has
# no swap; without this cap a test or build run that fills the memory makes the kernel evict the code pages of every
# process and read them back from the boot disk at the disk's limit, which stalls the whole VM for hours without an
# OOM kill: sshd answers no more, so neither Hunt nor the gateway reaches it. Capped, only the agent's processes reclaim
# and, past MemoryMax, the kernel kills the largest of them; sshd, Docker's databases and the guest agents keep the
# rest. The percentages are of the machine's memory, so they hold for every machine type a session VM may take.
[Unit]
Description=Processes of the agent on Hunt's session VM
Before=slices.target

[Slice]
MemoryAccounting=yes
MemoryHigh=80%
MemoryMax=85%
